   "updated": 1792584397639,
   "link": null,
   "locked": false,
   "text": "* Theoretical sizing. Current deployment: single user.\n\nAssumptions:\n- DAU: 1M\n- Reports per user/day: 3\n- Peak: 3 X average\n- Tier mix: 60% quick / 35% standard / 5% deep\n- Job duration: 1 / 4 / 10 min\n- Companies per report: 3 / 5 / 7\n- Standard report: ~250K tokens, ~30 searches, ~50KB stored\n- Hot companies: ~50K, cached <= 30 days, user-triggered refresh\n\nCalculations:\n- Traffic\n    1M DAU X 3 = 3M reports/day\n    3M / 86,400 = ~35/s avg -> ~100/s peak\n- Concurrency\n    Avg job: 0.6X1 + 0.35X4 + 0.05X10 = 2.5 min\n    100/s X 150s = ~15K concurrent jobs at peak\n- LLM tokens (quick 50K / standard 250K / deep 1M)\n    Avg: ~170K tokens/report\n    Peak: 100/s X 170K = ~17M tokens/sec\n- Search (quick 10 / standard 30 / deep 80)\n    ~20 searches/report avg -> ~2K searches/sec peak\n- Cost (quick $0.10 / standard $0.50 / deep $2)\n    Avg: ~$0.34/report -> ~$1M/day, ~$30M/month before cache\n- Storage\n    Sources stored once per company, reports reference them: ~50KB/report\n    3M X 50KB = 150GB/day X 30 = ~4.5TB/month\n- Cache size\n    50K companies X 750KB (deep) = 37.5GB -> ~40GB hot research set (Postgres)\n\nBottleneck: LLM and search APIs, not compute\n-> queue + cache + rate limiting",
   "originalText": "* Theoretical sizing. Current deployment: single user.\n\nAssumptions:\n- DAU: 1M\n- Reports per user/day: 3\n- Peak: 3 X average\n- Tier mix: 60% quick / 35% standard / 5% deep\n- Job duration: 1 / 4 / 10 min\n- Companies per report: 3 / 5 / 7\n- Standard report: ~250K tokens, ~30 searches, ~50KB stored\n- Hot companies: ~50K, cached <= 30 days, user-triggered refresh\n\nCalculations:\n- Traffic\n    1M DAU X 3 = 3M reports/day\n    3M / 86,400 = ~35/s avg -> ~100/s peak\n- Concurrency\n    Avg job: 0.6X1 + 0.35X4 + 0.05X10 = 2.5 min\n    100/s X 150s = ~15K concurrent jobs at peak\n- LLM tokens (quick 50K / standard 250K / deep 1M)\n    Avg: ~170K tokens/report\n    Peak: 100/s X 170K = ~17M tokens/sec\n- Search (quick 10 / standard 30 / deep 80)\n    ~20 searches/report avg -> ~2K searches/sec peak\n- Cost (quick $0.10 / standard $0.50 / deep $2)\n    Avg: ~$0.34/report -> ~$1M/day, ~$30M/month before cache\n- Storage\n    Sources stored once per company, reports reference them: ~50KB/report\n    3M X 50KB = 150GB/day X 30 = ~4.5TB/month\n- Cache size\n    50K companies X 750KB (deep) = 37.5GB -> ~40GB hot research set (Postgres)\n\nBottleneck: LLM and search APIs, not compute\n-> queue + cache + rate limiting",
   "fontSize": 20,
   "fontFamily": 5,
   "textAlign": "left",
   "verticalAlign": "top",
   "containerId": null,
   "autoResize": true,
   "lineHeight": 1.25,
